{"id": "msg_00d3fce99468499895140c9dd069696c", "role": "assistant", "parts": [{"type": "text", "text": "User wants total hours ≤ 48 for the week. Currently 77.5h. I need to scale down. Keeping ZenTao original titles (content option = keep). I'll adjust hourly allocation so the weekly total lands within 48h, keeping task hours reasonable and distributing bugs.\n\nThe sensible approach: keep the big real task hours as-is (they're substantial), and compress bug hours so total ≈ 48h. Let me compute: current task hours sum vs bug hours."}, {"type": "tool", "tool_id": "call_00_uaThUD36XpHAym41dSjb8381", "tool_name": "pwsh", "tool_uri": "", "skill_uri": "", "tool_status": "running", "tool_input": {"command": "cd \"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\Documents\\deepseek-harness\\default-workspace\"; python -c @\"\nimport openpyxl\nwb=openpyxl.load_workbook('研发-前端-田野-本周工作总结(2026.11.02-11.06).xlsx')\nws=wb.worksheets[0]\ntb=0;tt=0;nb=0;nt=0\nfor r in ws.iter_rows(min_row=3,values_only=True):\n    if r[0] is None: continue\n    h=float(r[8] or 0)\n    if str(r[4]).startswith('Bug'): tb+=h; nb+=1\n    else: tt+=h; nt+=1\nprint('bugs',nb,'bugHours',tb,'  tasks',nt,'taskHours',tt,'  total',tb+tt)\n\"@", "description": "Split bug vs task hours"}}], "created_at": "2026-11-06T08:12:56.434Z", "peer_id": "deepseek-harness-default-workspace"}
