{"id": "msg_0c309624a61e43efa8f57211f15e7694", "role": "assistant", "parts": [{"type": "text", "text": "Bugs=40h, tasks=37.5h, total 77.5h. Target ≤48h.\n\nTask hours (37.5h) are mostly real registered effort — but some inflated: 2101=16h, 2115=4h, 1497=4h, 2035=2h. That's already 26h in 4 tasks; with 48h cap the tasks alone eat most of it. The prior week's real report was ~60-70h though. But user explicitly wants ≤48h/week.\n\nBest approach: compress all rows so total = 48h, proportionally but keeping bugs at ≥0.5h each (min). 80 bugs × 0.5 = 40h minimum for bugs  — that alone plus 37.5h tasks > 48h. So I must also trim task hours.\n\nReasonable plan to hit ≤48h:\n- Bugs: reduce to 0.25h each? Unusual. Better: consolidate — but user said keep original titles (can't merge).\n- Realistically 80 bugs + 19 tasks in a 5-day week at ≤48h means avg ~0.5h/bug and trimmed tasks.\n\nLet me set: tasks capped/reduced to represent actual, bugs at 0.5h. Let me compute a scaling that keeps bug=0.4 and tasks scaled. Let me just proportionally scale everything by factor 48/77.5 = 0.619, then round to 0.5 grid, and re-check. I'll rebuild with scaled hours."}, {"type": "tool", "tool_id": "call_00_zwC19MuhDpr8kqKIkd3l2690", "tool_name": "pwsh", "tool_uri": "", "skill_uri": "", "tool_status": "running", "tool_input": {"command": "cd \"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\Documents\\deepseek-harness\\default-workspace\"; python -c @\"\nimport openpyxl\nwb=openpyxl.load_workbook('研发-前端-田野-本周工作总结(2026.11.02-11.06).xlsx')\nws=wb.worksheets[0]\nrows=[]\nfor r in ws.iter_rows(min_row=3,values_only=True):\n    if r[0] is None: continue\n    rows.append(list(r))\ntb=sum(float(r[8]) for r in rows if str(r[4]).startswith('Bug'))\ntt=sum(float(r[8]) for r in rows if not str(r[4]).startswith('Bug'))\nprint('cur',tb,tt,tb+tt)\n# Strategy: tasks scaled to 24h, bugs to 24h => total 48\ntscale=24.0/tt\nbscale=24.0/tb\n# set task hours by scale rounding to 0.5, min 0.5\nimport math\nnew=[]\nfor r in rows:\n    h=float(r[8])\n    if str(r[4]).startswith('Bug'):\n        nh=max(0.5, round(h*bscale*2)/2)\n    else:\n        nh=max(0.5, round(h*tscale*2)/2)\n    r[8]=nh\n    new.append(r)\ntb2=sum(r[8] for r in new if str(r[4]).startswith('Bug'))\ntt2=sum(r[8] for r in new if not str(r[4]).startswith('Bug'))\nprint('scaled bugs',tb2,'tasks',tt2,'total',tb2+tt2)\n\"@", "description": "Test scaling to 48h"}}], "created_at": "2026-11-06T08:13:02.200Z", "peer_id": "deepseek-harness-default-workspace"}
